# R30.M9-001 (#1085) — the AML fuzz regression corpus.
#
# Corpus entries are RAW AML BYTE STREAMS, not text. Marking them binary
# does two things that matter for a regression corpus:
#
#   - it stops any newline or encoding normalisation from touching them.
#     A corpus entry whose bytes were rewritten in transit is no longer
#     the input that produced the outcome recorded in MANIFEST.tsv, and
#     the replay gate would fail for a reason that has nothing to do with
#     the interpreter.
#
#   - it stops git from printing them as diffs. A byte-level diff of an
#     AML stream is unreadable, and the reviewable artefact is the
#     MANIFEST.tsv row — which IS text, and is deliberately not covered
#     by this rule.
*.aml binary
